#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""gym: workout log engine. Jefit CSV export or Open Training API -> local SQLite -> stats, review, charts.

Usage:
  gym import csv FILE [--unit kg|lb] [--dry-run] [--json]
                                      import a Jefit CSV export (multi-section file: SETTING, PROFILE,
                                      WORKOUT SESSIONS, EXERCISE LOGS, EXERCISE SET LOGS, CUSTOM EXERCISES, ...)
  gym sync [--since YYYY-MM-DD] [--dry-run] [--json]
                                      pull sessions through the Open Training API (read-only GETs, Bearer
                                      token): the first run takes the whole history, later runs re-read from
                                      7 days before the last stored session. Warm-up sets and cardio are skipped.
  gym sync --probe                    read-only probe of the API with the token: status codes and JSON key
                                      names only (never values, never the token) -> state dir probe.json;
                                      exit 1 when the token or an endpoint fails
  gym stats [--weeks N] [--end DATE] [--json]
                                      sessions/week, hard sets + tonnage per muscle per week, balance,
                                      PRs (e1RM), progression of the main lifts, streaks, gaps
  gym review [--weeks N] [--end DATE] [--if-trained DAYS] [--json]
                                      phone-sized card with 3 plan suggestions (not medical advice);
                                      --if-trained DAYS prints nothing unless a session lies in the last DAYS days
  gym chart [--weeks N] [--end DATE] [--out DIR]
                                      PNG charts (volume.png, e1rm.png, sessions.png) via Pillow; skipped
                                      when Pillow is missing. Prints one path per line.
  gym recap [--date D] [--json] | --cron
                                      post-workout recap: card of the last session; --cron (after sync) = one
                                      cue note in ~/inbox when a new session settled (no values in the note)
                                      (~/bin/lib/gymcoach.py)
  gym exercises [--json]              exercises with muscle group, equipment, pattern, kind, set count
  gym exercise NAME (--muscle M [--equipment E] | --reset)
                                      fix a classification (kept across imports) or go back to automatic
  gym status [--json]                 counts, date range, last import, token/API state (no workout values)
  gym plan draft [--days 2|3|4] [--goal mixed|strength|hypertrophy|fitness] [--minutes M] [--swap OLD=NEW]
                [--dry-run] [--json]
                                      training plan from the log: slots filled with exercises he actually does,
                                      start weights from recent e1RM, time budget per session -> plan state file
  gym plan show [--travel] [--json]   the plan card, push state, review due after 4 weeks (--travel: the
                                      travel plan's card)
  gym plan next [--json]              phone card of the next session (local data only, for /gym): the day after
                                      the one the last logged session matches, else the first; sets×reps @ weight,
                                      last session, weekly streak; no plan: the review's summary line. --json = the
                                      dashboard block (dash-data): sessions this week vs the plan's days/week, 8
                                      weekly counts, streak, next day + lead exercise, e1RM of squat/bench/deadlift
                                      (last + change vs 4 weeks before; per-session series), free evenings (or null),
                                      other_activity (dance: shuffle/rave count + hours, this week and 8 weeks)
  gym plan push [--travel] [--apply] [--rebuild] [--json]
                                      write the plan to Jefit as ONE routine "Assistant plan". Default: dry run
                                      printing the exact requests ({symbols} for ids). --apply: the first time a
                                      safe test (create/read/delete "Assistant test", his routines unchanged),
                                      then create or diff-update only that routine; read-back verified. Paced
                                      (GYM_WRITE_DELAY s between requests, default 1), HTTP 429 retried with
                                      Retry-After or 5-60 s backoff; a push that stopped half-way resumes from
                                      the live routine; leftover "Assistant plan/test" routines this tool
                                      created (journal) are deleted first. --rebuild: delete and recreate.
                                      The phone app shows changes only after its Sync (Progress tab)
  gym plan update [--write] [--apply] [--json]
                                      double progression from the sessions since the last update, swaps for
                                      lifts stalled or skipped 3 sessions; Jefit diff vs the last pushed version
                                      (sessions of applied return weeks are not progression data)
  gym plan travel [--from DATE --to DATE] [--days-per-week 2|3] [--minutes M] [--band] [--bar]
                [--dry-run] [--json]
                                      bodyweight plan for a trip (dates default to the trip under way or next
                                      in trip-conditions' trips.json, GYM_TRIPS): Jefit catalogue exercises
                                      standing in for his main lifts, 30-40 min, reps 1-2 short of failure;
                                      --band / --bar add band moves / pull-ups -> plan-travel.json.
                                      `gym plan push --travel` writes it as its own routine "Assistant travel"
                                      (same paced, resumable, allowlisted push; never "Assistant plan")
  gym plan return [--from DATE] [--apply [--week 1|2]] [--dry-run] [--json]
                                      re-entry for the 2 weeks after a trip (from: the travel plan's end + 1):
                                      week 1 -15 % of his last logged working weights and one set less, week 2
                                      -10 %, then the plan -> plan-return.json. Draft only; --apply writes that
                                      week into "Assistant plan" (default: the week under way, else 1);
                                      `gym plan push --apply` puts the plan weights back

Data model: sessions (date, start, duration) -> exercise logs -> sets (weight kg, reps, duration s, Epley
e1RM). Body stats from the export's PROFILE section. Weights are stored in kg (lb converted on import;
API set weights are always pounds, also for metric accounts).
Dedupe: a session is the same when its source id matches, else its start time (+-2 min), else (no start
time) the same date with a shared exercise. Re-importing unchanged sessions is a no-op; changed ones are
replaced. Exercises are matched by Jefit id, else by normalized name; renamed exercises keep their id.

Analysis rules: hard set = a working set: within 15 % of the session's best set for that exercise by Epley
e1RM (so warm-ups drop out); >= 50 % of the top reps / duration for bodyweight / timed sets. Muscle volume counts fractional sets (primary muscle
1, secondary muscles of compound lifts 0.5). e1RM = Epley on sets of 1-12 reps; bodyweight exercises use
best reps, timed ones the longest hold. Main lifts = compound weighted lifts with >= 4 sessions in the window.
Plateau = no e1RM PR for >= 4 weeks while still training the lift (>= 3 sessions since the PR).
Targets: 10-20 hard sets per muscle per week (evidence-based range); suggestions are heuristics.

Files (private health data; never into notes or public paths): DB ~/.local/state/gym/gym.db (0600),
charts ~/.local/state/gym/charts/, probe ~/.local/state/gym/probe.json, API settings ~/.config/gym/api.json
(0600; only values that differ from the defaults, e.g. the Jefit user id found through the token),
token ~/.secrets/jefit-token (0600, never printed; by handle "gym" through core.egress: hub mode needs no file,
local/shadow mode reads it). Body stats come from the CSV only.
Plan: ~/.local/state/gym/plan.json, plan-pushed.json (last pushed target + Jefit ids), plan-push.log (every
write), plan-history/; writes use ~/.secrets/jefit-token-rw when present (a Read + write token), else the token
(by handle "gym" through core.egress, like the reads; the hub's gym binding has write rules for these paths).
Other activity: shuffle dancing and rave nights from calcache titles (shuffle; rave/club/techno words or a
rave-radar artist, 2+ h), kept per event (date, kind, hours; no titles) in ~/.local/state/gym/activity.json (0600)
on every stats/review/plan next read, so past weeks keep them after they leave calcache's window. Shown next to
the sessions; never counted as gym in the streak, but a week with dance and no gym is 'active', not 'missed'.
Env (tests): GYM_DB, GYM_STATE_DIR, GYM_NOW (YYYY-MM-DD or YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM), GYM_CALCACHE, GYM_RAVE_RADAR, GYM_TOKEN_FILE, GYM_TOKEN_RW_FILE, GYM_WRITE_DELAY,
GYM_API_CONFIG, JEFIT_API_BASE,
OWNER_TZ.
Exit: 0 ok, 1 error (bad file, API/network), 2 usage, 3 no token, 4 API details pending.
"""
